   "exp": "Capital × months: A = 40,000×6 + 30,000×6 = 4,20,000; B = 60,000×8 = 4,80,000; C = 50,000×6 = 3,00,000. Ratio 42 : 48 : 30 = 7 : 8 : 5. B's share = 8/20 × 1,20,000 = ₹48,000. Trap: giving C 8 months (joins 'after 4 months' misread) or keeping A at ₹40,000 all year (A = 4,80,000 → B = ₹45,714).",
