   "exp": "|x| + |y − 2| ≤ 3 is a square (rhombus) centred at (0, 2) with vertices (±3, 2), (0, 5), (0, −1); its area = 2 × 3² = 18. The part below y = 0 is a small triangle with apex (0, −1); on y = 0, |x| ≤ 3 − 2 = 1, so its base runs from (−1, 0) to (1, 0): area ½ × 2 × 1 = 1. Required area = 18 − 1 = 17. Trap: taking the full 18, or mis-sizing the cut-off triangle (base 4 instead of 2 gives 16).",
